BandC wrote:
>
> Speaking of partly eaten corpses, I find that if I get interrupted
> eating something that is rotten, the rest of the food is always fresh
> when I eat it later. Is this intentional (it doesn't make sense if the
> first part is rotten, all should be rotten) or am I just very lucky?

The rest isn't fresh it just doesn't cause further problems.
The bit that's not obvious is that the rest ends up having
extremely little nutrition.

Non-corpse food items have a chance of being spoiled, and
spoiled food has a lot less nutrition than regular food.
It's yet another of the random events that happen in
Nethack.  When facing Famine in the astral plane, eating
a K-ration has the same chance of having little nutrition
as eating any other time in the game.  This is why K-rations
are so muc preferred over C-rations - Extra nutrition
during the one-turn eating process when it works better
makes up for the lower nutrition when it's spoiled.  With
C-rations it's too easy to fall gradually behind as you
fight Famine.



